%H A077055 Joe Sawada, <a href="https://www.socs.uoguelph.ca/~sawada/prog/stamp_meander.c">Stamp foldings, semi-meanders, and open meanders</a>, C program, 2008 (includes symmetric meanders).
%H A077055 Joe Sawada and Roy Li, <a href="https://doi.org/10.37236/2404">Stamp Foldings, Semi-Meanders, and Open Meanders: Fast Generation Algorithms</a>, The Electronic Journal of Combinatorics 19(2) (2012), #P43.
%F A077055 For n even a(n) = (A005316(n)+A005316(n/2))/2 (this is A078592).
%F A077055 For n odd a(n) = (A005316(n)+2*A223096(floor(n/2)))/4. - _Stéphane Legendre_, Apr 09 2013
%F A077055 From _Hunter Hogan_, Nov 16 2026: (Start)
%F A077055 a(2*n+1) = (A005315(n+1) + 2*A223096(n))/4.
%F A077055 Let T(n,k) = A400429(n,k).
%F A077055 a(2*n+1) = (T(2*n+1,1) + 2*A223096(n))/4.
%F A077055 a(2*n) = (T(2*n+1,1) - T(2*n,2) + (1 + (n mod 2))*T(n+1,1) - (1 - (n mod 2))*T(n,2))/4, for n >= 4. (End)
%e A077055 For n=7 the A005316(7) = 42 meanders with 7 crossings fall into 5 equivalence classes of size 2 and 8 of size 4, so a(7) = 5+8 = 13.
